-- CK-30: v1's evidence miscount in a declaration nothing reaches. `f` is an
-- unannotated recursive function with an `eq` constraint, and v1 passes the
-- recursive call `f x y (n - 1)` a different number of hidden arguments than
-- `f` takes (CK-30's miscount). `main` never uses `f`.
--
-- On 9a931d7 this built and ran, printing `x`: `Lower` met the miscount only
-- on code dead-code elimination kept, and `f` was not kept. Since R2a the I7
-- assert (checker-v2.md §13.1) walks every declaration at `check` time and
-- refuses the program with INTERNAL ERROR at the recursive call — a decision
-- the manager took on purpose (review of R2a, S1): the table is wrong whether
-- or not it is emitted, and v2 removes the miscount. Expected, once v2 counts
-- correctly: it builds and prints `x`, exactly what 9a931d7 printed.
import Node exposing (Program)


f x y n =
    if n == 0 then
        x == y

    else
        f x y (n - 1)


main : Program
main =
    Node.printLines [ "x" ]
